# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.vercel

# claude code local state — never committed
.claude/

# EXPERIMENTAL sherpa-onnx WASM/model assets (~205MB) — lab/dev-only, per
# sherpaOnnxProvider.ts's own ASSET DEPLOYMENT doc comment. Never committed:
# too large for version control, and never meant to ship to operators.
/public/sherpa-onnx-lab/

# whisper.cpp command.wasm WASM/model assets (~33MB) ARE committed —
# see whisperCppProvider.ts's own ASSET DEPLOYMENT doc comment for the
# compelling, documented reason (browser-level `new Worker(url)` same-
# origin security cannot be satisfied by a cross-origin CDN like Vercel
# Blob for this specific multi-threaded WASM build, confirmed by direct
# testing 2026-08-20 — unlike sherpa-onnx, which has no such requirement).
# 33MB is comfortably under Vercel's 100MB Hobby/1GB Pro source-upload
# limit, unlike sherpa-onnx's ~204MB bundle.

# vosk-model-small-en-us-0.15 (Apache-2.0, ~39.3MB, repacked as a gzipped
# tar with a top-level "model/" dir per vosk-browser's documented format;
# sha256 8067729ab10947eed53a0571d1956e4834f22f650c7a7e1dbf3cd3dfa24d4633)
# IS committed — see voskProvider.ts's own ASSET DEPLOYMENT doc comment. The
# vosk-browser WASM RUNTIME is NOT a separate committed asset: unlike
# whisper.cpp/sherpa-onnx, it's imported as an ordinary npm package
# (single-threaded — no SharedArrayBuffer/pthread/COOP/COEP requirement,
# confirmed by inspecting the published bundle) and bundled by Next.js like
# any other dependency; its own Worker is spawned from a same-origin
# blob: URL embedded in that bundle, never a cross-origin script URL, so
# none of Whisper's `new Worker(crossOriginUrl)` SecurityError applies. No
# Vercel Blob credentials were available this round to host the model
# externally (unlike sherpa-onnx); ~39.3MB is comfortably under Vercel's
# 100MB source-upload limit, so direct commit is the same accepted fallback
# already used for whisper-cpp-lab.
